  <name>Mise Browser</name>
  <summary>Keyboard-centric web browser engineered for Linux</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      Mise Browser is an intentional, efficient web browser built for Linux. Engineered for fanless hardware and resource efficiency, Mise replaces tab bloat with true DOM detachment hibernation and containerised workspace isolation.
    </p>
    <p>Key highlights include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Keyboard-driven navigation: modal keybindings and link hinting for mouse-free browsing</li>
      <li>Containerised workspaces: discrete session partitions keeping profiles separated</li>
      <li>Tab hibernation: true DOM detachment releasing system memory from idle tabs</li>
      <li>Built-in adblocking: native network-level request filtering without extension bloat</li>
      <li>Tokyo Night interface: clean vertical sidebar with light and dark mode support</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
